Under the Constitution, the purpose of the Court of Appeals (CA) is to review:
* Decisions and orders of the Regional Trial Courts nationwide;
* Decisions and orders of the Court of Tax Appeals;
* Awards, judgments, final orders, or resolutions of, or authorized by, 21 Quasi-Judicial Agencies exercising quasi-judicial functions (as mentioned in Rule 43 of the 1997 Rules of Civil Procedure);
* The National Amnesty Commission; and
* The Office of the Ombudsman.
